---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import { blogArticles } from '../../blog/articles';
import { SITE } from '../../seo/site';

const article = blogArticles[0];
const title = `${article.titleEn} A Beginner’s Guide | ${SITE.name}`;
const description = article.summaryEn;
const canonical = `${SITE.origin}${article.href}`;
const sourceUrl = article.sourceUrl;
const jungleImage = 'https://cmsassets.rgpub.io/sanity/images/dsfx7636/news/ed4bef5c2369044d76cf535e038b6c1f8d323f13-3288x2100.png?accountingTag=LoL';
const laneImage = 'https://cmsassets.rgpub.io/sanity/images/dsfx7636/news/fc8d0c8c803a8e91a1912df9054b3be90211a2d9-3288x2100.png?accountingTag=LoL';
const jsonLd = [
  {
    '@context': 'https://schema.org',
    '@type': 'BlogPosting',
    headline: article.titleEn,
    description,
    image: article.coverUrl,
    datePublished: article.publishedAt,
    dateModified: article.publishedAt,
    mainEntityOfPage: canonical,
    author: { '@type': 'Organization', name: SITE.name, url: `${SITE.origin}/` },
    publisher: { '@type': 'Organization', name: SITE.name, url: `${SITE.origin}/` },
  },
  {
    '@context': 'https://schema.org',
    '@type': 'BreadcrumbList',
    itemListElement: [
      { '@type': 'ListItem', position: 1, name: 'Home', item: `${SITE.origin}/` },
      { '@type': 'ListItem', position: 2, name: 'Blog', item: `${SITE.origin}/blog/` },
      { '@type': 'ListItem', position: 3, name: article.titleEn, item: canonical },
    ],
  },
];
---
<BaseLayout {title} {description} {canonical} image={article.coverUrl} {jsonLd}>
  <nav class="blog-breadcrumbs" aria-label="Breadcrumb" data-aria-en="Breadcrumb" data-aria-zh="面包屑">
    <a href="/" data-en="Home" data-zh="首页">Home</a><span>/</span><a href="/blog/" data-en="Blog" data-zh="博客">Blog</a><span>/</span><span aria-current="page" data-en="Guide" data-zh="指南">Guide</span>
  </nav>

  <article class="blog-article" data-language-content="en">
    <header class="article-header">
      <p class="kicker">BEGINNER’S GUIDE</p>
      <h1>{article.titleEn}</h1>
      <p class="article-deck">A journey through Summoner’s Rift, from choosing a champion to working with four teammates toward the enemy Nexus.</p>
      <p class="article-meta"><time datetime={article.publishedAt}>July 19, 2026</time><span>·</span><span>{article.readingMinutes} min read</span></p>
    </header>
    <figure>
      <img src={article.coverUrl} alt={article.coverAltEn} data-alt-en={article.coverAltEn} data-alt-zh={article.coverAltZh} data-fallback="/placeholder.svg" data-placeholder="/placeholder.svg" width="3288" height="2100" loading="eager" decoding="async" />
      <figcaption>The blue team’s Nexus—the structure a team must defend. Image: <a href={sourceUrl} target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">Riot Games</a>.</figcaption>
    </figure>
    <section><h2>A team strategy game</h2><p>League of Legends is a competitive, team-based strategy game. Two teams of five each control a single champion, a character with a distinct set of abilities, strengths, and weaknesses. A match rewards mechanical skill, but it also asks players to read the map, share information, manage limited resources, and coordinate decisions.</p><p>Most new players begin on Summoner’s Rift, the game’s best-known map. No two matches play exactly alike: champion combinations, player choices, and a frequently updated ruleset create new situations from the opening minute to the final push.</p></section>
    <section><h2>Summoner’s Rift and the Nexus</h2><p>Each team begins in a base built around a Nexus. The straightforward win condition is to reach and destroy the opposing Nexus before the enemy destroys yours. Three lanes connect the bases, while a jungle full of neutral monsters and paths fills the space between them.</p><p>Turrets guard each lane, so teams usually advance with waves of allied minions. Destroying structures opens the map, creates safer routes forward, and turns a collection of small advantages into access to the enemy base.</p></section>
    <figure><img src={jungleImage} alt="Baron Nashor in the Summoner’s Rift jungle" data-alt-en="Baron Nashor in the Summoner’s Rift jungle" data-alt-zh="召唤师峡谷野区中的纳什男爵" data-fallback="/placeholder.svg" data-placeholder="/placeholder.svg" width="3288" height="2100" loading="lazy" decoding="async" /><figcaption>Baron Nashor is a major neutral objective that can help a team strengthen its push. Image: <a href={sourceUrl} target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">Riot Games</a>.</figcaption></figure>
    <section><h2>Five players, five positions</h2><p>A common team composition places one player in top lane, one in the jungle, one in mid lane, and two in bottom lane as a bot laner and support. These positions are not rigid identities, but they give a team a practical way to divide early resources and responsibilities.</p><p>With more than 170 champions, there is room for very different playstyles: durable frontliners, precise marksmen, explosive mages, mobile assassins, fighters, and allies who protect or empower the team. Learning one approachable champion and one position is often the easiest way to begin.</p></section>
    <figure><img src={laneImage} alt="A top lane champion on Summoner’s Rift" data-alt-en="A top lane champion on Summoner’s Rift" data-alt-zh="召唤师峡谷上路的一名英雄" data-fallback="/placeholder.svg" data-placeholder="/placeholder.svg" width="3288" height="2100" loading="lazy" decoding="async" /><figcaption>Different positions favour different responsibilities and champion styles. Image: <a href={sourceUrl} target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">Riot Games</a>.</figcaption></figure>
    <section><h2>How a match gains momentum</h2><p>Champions earn experience to level up and gold to buy items. Players gather those resources from minions, monsters, structures, and combat, then decide when to stay in lane, return to base, help a teammate, or contest an objective such as a dragon or Baron Nashor.</p><p>Kills matter, but they are usually a means to gain time and control. Strong teams convert a won fight into something lasting: a turret, an objective, deeper vision, or the final route to the Nexus. Communication and timing make individual plays add up.</p></section>
    <section><h2>A game that keeps evolving</h2><p>Riot Games regularly adjusts champions, items, systems, and seasonal goals. Beyond competition, League has grown through Runeterra’s stories, music, animation, character art, and a global esports scene. Players can enjoy it as a strategic sport, a social game with friends, or a doorway into a much larger fictional world.</p><p>If you want to learn the controls and current basics, continue with Riot Games’ official <a href={sourceUrl} target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">How to Play guide</a>.</p></section>
  </article>

  <article class="blog-article" data-language-content="zh">
    <header class="article-header"><p class="kicker">新手指南</p><h1>{article.titleZh}</h1><p class="article-deck">从选择英雄开始，走进召唤师峡谷，与四名队友一起向敌方水晶枢纽推进。</p><p class="article-meta"><time datetime={article.publishedAt}>2026 年 7 月 19 日</time><span>·</span><span>阅读约 {article.readingMinutes} 分钟</span></p></header>
    <figure><img src={article.coverUrl} alt={article.coverAltZh} data-alt-en={article.coverAltEn} data-alt-zh={article.coverAltZh} data-fallback="/placeholder.svg" data-placeholder="/placeholder.svg" width="3288" height="2100" loading="eager" decoding="async" /><figcaption>蓝色方的水晶枢纽——每支队伍都必须守护的核心建筑。图片来源：<a href={sourceUrl} target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">Riot Games</a>。</figcaption></figure>
    <section><h2>团队策略游戏</h2><p>《英雄联盟》是一款强调团队协作的竞技策略游戏。双方各有五名玩家，每人控制一位拥有独特技能、优势与弱点的英雄。操作能力很重要，但观察地图、共享信息、分配资源与协同行动同样决定胜负。</p><p>大多数新玩家会从召唤师峡谷开始。英雄组合、临场选择与持续更新的规则让每场对局从开局到最终推进都可能出现不同局面。</p></section>
    <section><h2>召唤师峡谷与水晶枢纽</h2><p>双方基地都围绕水晶枢纽建立。胜利目标十分直接：在己方枢纽被摧毁之前攻入敌方基地并摧毁对方枢纽。三条分路连接两座基地，分路之间则是遍布中立野怪与通道的野区。</p><p>防御塔守护着每条分路，玩家通常需要跟随己方小兵推进。拆除建筑可以打开地图空间、创造更安全的前进路线，并把一次次小优势转化为进入敌方基地的机会。</p></section>
    <figure><img src={jungleImage} alt="召唤师峡谷野区中的纳什男爵" data-alt-en="Baron Nashor in the Summoner’s Rift jungle" data-alt-zh="召唤师峡谷野区中的纳什男爵" data-fallback="/placeholder.svg" data-placeholder="/placeholder.svg" width="3288" height="2100" loading="lazy" decoding="async" /><figcaption>纳什男爵是重要的中立地图目标，击败它能显著增强团队推进能力。图片来源：<a href={sourceUrl} target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">Riot Games</a>。</figcaption></figure>
    <section><h2>五名玩家，五个位置</h2><p>常见阵容由一名上路、一名打野、一名中路，以及下路的输出位和辅助位组成。这些位置不是僵硬的身份限制，而是一种在前期合理分配资源与职责的方式。</p><p>游戏拥有超过 170 位英雄，涵盖坚韧的前排、精准的射手、爆发型法师、灵活的刺客、持续作战的战士，以及保护或强化队友的辅助。新手通常可以先选择一位容易理解的英雄和一个位置，逐步熟悉游戏。</p></section>
    <figure><img src={laneImage} alt="召唤师峡谷上路的一名英雄" data-alt-en="A top lane champion on Summoner’s Rift" data-alt-zh="召唤师峡谷上路的一名英雄" data-fallback="/placeholder.svg" data-placeholder="/placeholder.svg" width="3288" height="2100" loading="lazy" decoding="async" /><figcaption>不同位置承担不同职责，也适合不同类型的英雄。图片来源：<a href={sourceUrl} target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">Riot Games</a>。</figcaption></figure>
    <section><h2>一场对局如何积累优势</h2><p>英雄通过经验值提升等级，并使用金币购买装备。玩家可以从小兵、野怪、防御建筑与战斗中获得资源，再判断何时留在线上、回城补给、支援队友，或争夺巨龙与纳什男爵等地图目标。</p><p>击杀很重要，但它通常是争取时间与控制权的手段。成熟的团队会把一场胜利的团战转化为长期收益：防御塔、地图目标、更深入的视野，或通往水晶枢纽的最后一条道路。沟通与时机让个人操作真正汇聚成团队优势。</p></section>
    <section><h2>持续进化的游戏</h2><p>Riot Games 会持续调整英雄、装备、系统与赛季目标。在竞技之外，《英雄联盟》还通过符文之地的故事、音乐、动画、角色美术与全球电竞赛事不断扩展。玩家既可以把它当作策略竞技项目，也可以与朋友共同游玩，或把它视为进入宏大幻想世界的入口。</p><p>想了解当前版本的操作与基础规则，可以继续阅读 Riot Games 官方的<a href={sourceUrl} target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">新手玩法指南</a>。</p></section>
  </article>

  <style>
    .blog-breadcrumbs,.blog-article { width:min(900px,calc(100% - (var(--page-gutter) * 2))); margin-inline:auto; }
    .blog-breadcrumbs { display:flex; gap:9px; padding:28px 0 0; color:var(--muted); font-size:.84rem; white-space:nowrap; overflow-x:auto; }
    .blog-article { padding:clamp(52px,8vw,90px) 0 110px; }
    .article-header { max-width:820px; margin-bottom:42px; }
    .article-header h1 { font-family:Georgia,"Noto Serif SC",serif; font-size:clamp(2.7rem,6vw,5rem); line-height:1.05; font-weight:500; margin:.34em 0 .35em; overflow-wrap:anywhere; }
    .article-deck { color:#c7cad4; font-size:clamp(1.05rem,2vw,1.25rem); line-height:1.7; }
    .article-meta { display:flex; flex-wrap:wrap; gap:9px; color:var(--muted); font-size:.8rem; }
    .blog-article section { max-width:720px; margin:54px auto 0; }
    .blog-article h2 { font-family:Georgia,"Noto Serif SC",serif; color:var(--gold); font-size:clamp(1.65rem,3.3vw,2.25rem); line-height:1.2; margin:0 0 18px; }
    .blog-article section p { color:#c7cad4; font-size:1.06rem; line-height:1.9; margin:0 0 1.2em; }
    .blog-article section a,.blog-article figcaption a { color:var(--gold); text-decoration:underline; text-underline-offset:3px; }
    .blog-article a:focus-visible { outline:2px solid var(--gold); outline-offset:3px; }
    .blog-article figure { margin:46px 0 0; }
    .blog-article figure img { display:block; width:100%; height:auto; aspect-ratio:3288/2100; object-fit:cover; border:1px solid var(--line); background:#15182a; box-shadow:0 22px 64px #0007; }
    .blog-article figcaption { color:var(--muted); font-size:.78rem; line-height:1.6; margin-top:10px; overflow-wrap:anywhere; }
    @media (max-width:767px) {
      .blog-breadcrumbs { padding-top:18px; }
      .blog-article { padding:42px 0 76px; }
      .article-header { margin-bottom:28px; }
      .article-header h1 { font-size:clamp(2.35rem,12vw,3.4rem); }
      .blog-article section { margin-top:40px; }
      .blog-article section p { font-size:1rem; line-height:1.78; }
      .blog-article figure { width:calc(100% + (var(--page-gutter) * 2)); margin:34px calc(var(--page-gutter) * -1) 0; }
      .blog-article figcaption { padding-inline:var(--page-gutter); }
    }
  </style>
</BaseLayout>
